---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { path, REPO_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  page="privacy/"
  description="What Claude Overview reads on your machine, what it stores, and the only places it sends anything."
  lede="Claude Overview has no server and no analytics. It talks to four services, and only those you give it a key for beyond the first."
>
  <h2>Who handles the network</h2>
  <p>
    The app's Rust core makes every network call and holds every key. The windows you see only draw what the core
    sends them; they never see a key and never call out themselves.
  </p>

  <h2>What leaves your machine, and where it goes</h2>
  <div class="co-table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>When</th><th>What is sent</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>status.claude.com</td>
          <td>Every 2 minutes</td>
          <td>A plain request for the public status feed. No key, nothing about you.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>api.anthropic.com</td>
          <td>Every 30 minutes with an Admin key; every 5 minutes with an API key</td>
          <td>Your Admin key, to read this credit period's spend from the Usage and Cost Analytics API. Your API key, to list Message Batches. Only if you add them.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>api.github.com</td>
          <td>Every 5 minutes with a token</td>
          <td>Your GitHub token, to search for open pull requests waiting for your review or opened by Claude Code. Only if you add one.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>github.com</td>
          <td>Once a day</td>
          <td>A request for the latest release's <code>latest.json</code>, and the package itself when you choose <em>Install and restart</em>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Each key goes only to the service it belongs to. Nothing is sent to me or to anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>What it reads on your machine</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Claude Code's transcripts, under <code>~/.claude/projects</code> (or the folder you set). It reads the usage on each
      line: model, tokens, time and project. The transcripts are read where they are and never sent anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      Claude Code's <code>settings.json</code>, only when you add or remove the hooks, to
      add or take out its own three entries. A backup is kept beside it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it stores</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A small SQLite database in the app's data folder: the usage it has read (kept for 90 days), how far it has read each
      transcript, your settings, the last good API credit figures, and which alerts it has already sent.
    </li>
    <li>
      Marker files in the same folder, written by the Claude Code hooks when a session is waiting, and removed when the
      session moves on or ends.
    </li>
    <li>
      Keys and the GitHub token in the OS keychain (Keychain, Credential Manager or the Secret Service), never in the
      database or a file. Settings shows only their last four characters, and removing one there deletes it from the keychain.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Removing it</h2>
  <p>
    Remove the Claude Code hooks in Settings before you uninstall, and remove each key there too: that deletes it from
    the keychain. Then uninstall the app and delete its data folder.
  </p>

  <h2>Checking this</h2>
  <p>
    The app is open source under the MIT licence. Every network call is in the Rust core, in
    <a href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/main/src-tauri/src`}><code>src-tauri/src</code></a>, and <a href={path('settings/')}>Settings</a>
    lists each key and what it is for.
  </p>
</Doc>
